{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792506603,"nonce":"keUbN6v78o0eLe6SoBF7zAHgvx0=","message":"Implemented CodeEditor/CodeView find and replace in d20b585, with a platform-modifier guard in 993438d. The compact floating panel uses theme-tinted frosted glass and responsive bounds. It includes case/whole-word/regex toggles, visible match marks, wrapped navigation, single replacement and atomic Replace All through the existing undo/edit APIs, plus invalid-pattern errors. Bare Haxe regex patterns are the primary input; ~/pattern/flags is optional, and regex replacements accept capture references.\n\nCodeFindState retains only input/option signals in CodeEditorState. Mounted owners contain the compiled expression, subject cache, result offsets and lazy controls; closing or unmounting releases these. Visible highlight rectangles are bounded and reused, and text edits do not jump the caret. Replace actions synchronize against current text/options before applying offsets, including events received in one batch. Read-only and disabled guards are enforced separately from the programmatic applyEdits API. findShortcuts=false allows applications to supply their keymap. Extra modifiers leave application shortcuts such as fullscreen available.\n\nValidation: CodeFindTest passed in both schemes, including Haxe flags, escaped slashes, captures, invalid regex, Unicode/zero-width boundaries, narrow panel bounds, wrapped/folded/offscreen navigation, same-batch replacement, undo/redo, read-only/disabled guards, remount/disposal and modifier handling. Existing CodeComponents passed all 274 checks, and CodeStateLifecycle passed. RayDE dark/light find snapshots passed for bare regex, captures, both replacement actions, undo, dirty state, tab remount and malformed-pattern recovery. No native API changes or new Cargo build tree are required for the component.","files":null}]}